{% from "govuk/components/details/macro.njk" import govukDetails %}

<p class="govuk-body">If Planning Inspectors decide that written representations are not enough to reach a decision, a public hearing may be scheduled.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">You do not commit to attending by choosing 'Yes', and you can change your mind later. We will send you details if a hearing is scheduled.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">You do not have to attend for your comments to be considered.</p>

{% set whatIsAHearing %}
	<p class="govuk-body">A hearing is a structured, face-to-face meeting. It's run as a round-table discussion led by an independent planning inspector.</p>
	<p class="govuk-body">At the start of the hearing, the inspector will:</p>
	<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
		<li>explain the details of the application</li>
		<li>state the main issues to be resolved</li>
		<li>list the specific topics that need further explanation</li>
	</ul>
	<p class="govuk-body">The inspector will then lead a discussion on each topic. They will ask direct questions to both sides to better understand the case.</p>
	<p class="govuk-body">Most hearings last between half a day and a full day. They usually conclude with the inspector visiting the development site.</p>
{% endset %}
{{ govukDetails({
	summaryText: "What is a hearing?",
	html: whatIsAHearing
}) }}
